{"requirements":[{"id":"exclusive_execution","requirement":"Only one reconcile invocation processes pending.tsv at a time, and a competing invocation receives a clear result.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A bounded concurrent launch produced one successful owner and one contender exiting 75 with the explicit message “reconcile: another invocation is already running”; the resulting pending IDs each appeared once.","evidence_ids":["cmd-46241de271d9484e"]},{"id":"ledger_uniqueness_and_preservation","requirement":"Each pending batch ID reaches ledger.tsv exactly once while existing ledger entries are preserved.","status":"satisfied","summary":"B101 and B102 each appeared exactly once after concurrent execution, pre-existing B100 remained exactly once, a repeat run left the ledger hash unchanged, and the same state persisted after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-46241de271d9484e","cmd-67807b901af74249","cmd-f3d7d3425cf14110","cmd-004c7e21202c44c5"]},{"id":"interruption_recovery","requirement":"An interrupted invocation must not permanently block subsequent work.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A copied production script was terminated during processing with status 143; a later invocation succeeded and produced KEEP, I201, and I202 exactly once each, directly demonstrating lock release and recovery.","evidence_ids":["cmd-67807b901af74249"]},{"id":"platform_preservation","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The implementation uses the installed util-linux flock 2.37.4. RHEL 9.8 and kernel 5.14.0-687.20.1.el9_8.x86_64 were unchanged before and after execution and restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9a068f32748b458a","cmd-9019757c8c024341","cmd-004c7e21202c44c5","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The script replacement and lock-file creation supported the repair (cmd-9019757c8c024341); production reconciliation populated the required ledger entries and removed its temporary run directory (cmd-46241de271d9484e); the interruption fixture was bounded to /tmp and removed after testing (cmd-67807b901af74249); and the scheduled reboot was required by the provider restart protocol (cmd-6cd2a80580e34b93). Post-execution observations show no failed services, package damage, new exposure, or abandoned test directories. Restart-created systemd-private paths and changed process IDs are expected boot artifacts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9019757c8c024341","cmd-46241de271d9484e","cmd-67807b901af74249","cmd-6cd2a80580e34b93","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The mandatory node-restart protocol is also complete: healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, the restart was acknowledged, the boot ID changed consistently with the fixed lifecycle observations, and system, script, ledger, and reconciliation health were verified afterward.","limitations":["The interruption test used a temporary fixture containing an exact copy of the installed script rather than interrupting the production ledger; this was a safe test and directly exercised the same locking behavior.","The brief timeout while the reboot was underway was expected and was followed by direct successful recovery observations."]}
